{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","id":"pg_3df0193dbabe55aa8130c2ceefa06cb4","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kenn-io-kata-docs-reference-configuration-md-f41a33383aba-c2ceefa06cb4.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1931f2a1efd75e7d81f9b7e86b81bde5"],"title":"kenn-io/kata/docs/reference/configuration.md @ f41a33383aba","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_16169b53e2cc0e4832f4a8f9eee939ee0aa5b6f4c8d37ddc2a7e78cae1340972"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Clients auto-start a local daemon when none is reachable; an autostart_idle_timeout lets such a narrowly scoped daemon exit after foreground use stops, while explicit daemons remain long-running."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2cb762dd951f0df0bc2aa614f13ca8aa4c7feaf13a95ec1136cdf1683d910641"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On an idle-enabled auto-start daemon, scheduled work is opportunistic: timers do not keep the process resident, so continuous sync, federation, timed claims, embeddings, or hooks need an explicit service-managed daemon."}],"claim_ids":["clm_16169b53e2cc0e4832f4a8f9eee939ee0aa5b6f4c8d37ddc2a7e78cae1340972","clm_2cb762dd951f0df0bc2aa614f13ca8aa4c7feaf13a95ec1136cdf1683d910641"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","id":"pg_71c1b5ba40585300afd4d3eda87cf2ba","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kenn-io-kata-docs-design-autostart-idle-shutdown-md-f41a33383aba-d3eda87cf2ba.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_c2d21531c29051979a0326fc4156b243"],"title":"kenn-io/kata/docs/design/autostart-idle-shutdown.md @ f41a33383aba","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0069618a1905deb33c4a79b04f7b94e692c96adbd183f122581c028cddf9779a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Closing an issue is an explicit API mutation carrying a reason, message, typed evidence, and actor attribution; kata never infers closure from git history."},{"claim_ids":["clm_00e40100e2d03306aae4a59f12b46d255a26fd1fb10d9dd744ec3f3b94cdeb7f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"By default issue state lives in a local SQLite database under KATA_HOME; teams can opt into a remote daemon or federation, and a shared daemon can use Postgres via KATA_DSN."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22c69789f13d00e4cc72b49dc5ad28928c01efea182316a37a049d6e99ab22d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers agent-oriented ergonomics: stable short refs, --json and --agent output, idempotent creates, semantic-aware search, a claim flow, and predictable failure modes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2a93491b1c047b51d85a89b0e727b42c6a4d70169445e82ef1e16ead53e4c486"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All reads and writes go through kata's HTTP API; no client opens SQLite or Postgres directly, and a Go app can mount the listener-free service in-process."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2ea7f8f489d5b6ec35b8382ef7a8e28bf02a6179c72919e880d6269ccf334bea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata is a durable task ledger for coding agents and humans: agents create, claim, relate, and close issues with evidence via CLI, while humans supervise in a terminal UI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4e78ed48a486b339474f3c80394ef7cb852392df2973ed88bd44f00e912a91e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata uses pure-Go SQLite via modernc.org/sqlite with no CGO, a Huma-based HTTP API over a Unix socket, and claims no runtime dependencies beyond the single binary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_668d7dd62c30f29502c922545840f93b4560fba604e36c08db8b26a90b460872"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata init --with-agents writes a managed briefing into AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md without overwriting existing content, and --with-codex-hooks installs structured Codex SessionStart hooks in .codex/hooks.json."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7558ec539179c9b0b5fb17d46dba15625093c92aca35bbcbfbbfb1866c250621"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships as one Go binary with a CLI, a long-lived daemon, a TUI, and a browser UI served by the daemon with no separate backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7dbb4dd46e57259ad759c2c67680af5cc34dab6e9cfbd95fda4154a0cd21a92f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata is intentionally not a project-management suite, git workflow engine, agent worker pool, or SaaS tracker; it does not ride git remotes for sharing, relying on the remote daemon and federation instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_960e338f85662cc0c11127b6beb4ae253fe01e2900c159e686918c1478ef2d5a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors should see docs/development/contributing.md for repository layout and local checks including make test, make lint, make vet, and make nilaway."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba58060823cb522ae4a6d787c5fda77807758d646cc0968665252665c62fd0eb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata quickstart (alias kata agent-instructions) prints an operating contract for coding agents: search before creating, pass idempotency keys, prefer --agent output, claim work, and close only verified work with evidence."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ea2766fb551d3f1dade01d0efad98044e1306d493c4a47acb41a524aee85aab8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building from source requires Go 1.27 or later; module-source installs include the CLI, daemon, and TUI but not the compiled browser bundle needed for `kata ui`."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0069618a1905deb33c4a79b04f7b94e692c96adbd183f122581c028cddf9779a","clm_00e40100e2d03306aae4a59f12b46d255a26fd1fb10d9dd744ec3f3b94cdeb7f","clm_22c69789f13d00e4cc72b49dc5ad28928c01efea182316a37a049d6e99ab22d5","clm_2a93491b1c047b51d85a89b0e727b42c6a4d70169445e82ef1e16ead53e4c486","clm_2ea7f8f489d5b6ec35b8382ef7a8e28bf02a6179c72919e880d6269ccf334bea","clm_4e78ed48a486b339474f3c80394ef7cb852392df2973ed88bd44f00e912a91e4","clm_668d7dd62c30f29502c922545840f93b4560fba604e36c08db8b26a90b460872","clm_7558ec539179c9b0b5fb17d46dba15625093c92aca35bbcbfbbfb1866c250621","clm_7dbb4dd46e57259ad759c2c67680af5cc34dab6e9cfbd95fda4154a0cd21a92f","clm_960e338f85662cc0c11127b6beb4ae253fe01e2900c159e686918c1478ef2d5a","clm_ba58060823cb522ae4a6d787c5fda77807758d646cc0968665252665c62fd0eb","clm_ea2766fb551d3f1dade01d0efad98044e1306d493c4a47acb41a524aee85aab8"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","id":"pg_7484f634bbdd52f5ad357e3f79aea17f","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kenn-io-kata-readme-md-f41a33383aba-7e3f79aea17f.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe"],"title":"kenn-io/kata/README.md @ f41a33383aba","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_0069618a1905deb33c4a79b04f7b94e692c96adbd183f122581c028cddf9779a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Closing an issue is an explicit API mutation carrying a reason, message, typed evidence, and actor attribution; kata never infers closure from git history."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1d761045d120ea8923262dbdeef993672c801706f18f46f8bb703e82304d9a4b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every state change appends to an immutable event log with the actor recorded; actors are free-form snapshots on events, not foreign keys, and there is no global user registry."},{"claim_ids":["clm_22c69789f13d00e4cc72b49dc5ad28928c01efea182316a37a049d6e99ab22d5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers agent-oriented ergonomics: stable short refs, --json and --agent output, idempotent creates, semantic-aware search, a claim flow, and predictable failure modes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2a93491b1c047b51d85a89b0e727b42c6a4d70169445e82ef1e16ead53e4c486"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All reads and writes go through kata's HTTP API; no client opens SQLite or Postgres directly, and a Go app can mount the listener-free service in-process."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3d3002806729950234aaffc9759ad092cfbd88ac69489d08cef8df52280d327b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Workspace identity derives from the normalized git remote URL rather than the filesystem path, so clones resolve to the same project; one git repository attaches to exactly one project."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3e3425fb2166eb68f9fdb901185b35e92b3106eab6b25f1057027a73901f37c1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The surface is deliberately small: three relationship types, labels, owners, comments, and a constrained integer priority 0-4; there is no in_progress status, severity field, threaded replies, reactions, attachments, or markdown rendering."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4e78ed48a486b339474f3c80394ef7cb852392df2973ed88bd44f00e912a91e4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"kata uses pure-Go SQLite via modernc.org/sqlite with no CGO, a Huma-based HTTP API over a Unix socket, and claims no runtime dependencies beyond the single binary."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6535b61aee64a46d6b5d041021467c3238e8df80651fc688e233d709c10108e2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Permanent non-goals include workspace-local behavior overrides, per-issue SSE subscriptions, bulk mutation endpoints, remote webhooks, and a (kata-#N) commit-message convention."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7558ec539179c9b0b5fb17d46dba15625093c92aca35bbcbfbbfb1866c250621"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships as one Go binary with a CLI, a long-lived daemon, a TUI, and a browser UI served by the daemon with no separate backend."},{"claim_ids":["clm_89e6452e8b4e8fd72736a2a91c39c87bf02b8a3ac5d94656580e0409a83deccc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The loopback HTTP server rejects non-empty Origin headers, requires application/json Content-Type on mutations, and emits no CORS headers to resist drive-by browser requests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8c52c55eccbd5b2c6970defb70c71ad8b502d7ea2e24c19825928526eb60a8e3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Local mode trusts the OS user with no authentication on a Unix socket or loopback listener; shared/remote modes require a bearer token and explicit trust opt-in before credentials cross a plaintext non-loopback connection."},{"claim_ids":["clm_970a78ae79337d59265c6517bb5db2f6b618efc17772bf26735c3df95c7e145b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hooks run local commands after database commit on a bounded worker pool, invoked without a shell via exec.Command with event data as JSON on stdin; hooks are not a sandbox and run with the daemon's OS user."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a667136be04ff445a4314681169935c2946185001a53320c731d2f92174a6d3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Projects are bound to workspaces explicitly via a committed .kata.toml, never inferred from the current directory; outside a bound workspace every command except kata init fails with project_not_initialized."}],"claim_ids":["clm_0069618a1905deb33c4a79b04f7b94e692c96adbd183f122581c028cddf9779a","clm_1d761045d120ea8923262dbdeef993672c801706f18f46f8bb703e82304d9a4b","clm_22c69789f13d00e4cc72b49dc5ad28928c01efea182316a37a049d6e99ab22d5","clm_2a93491b1c047b51d85a89b0e727b42c6a4d70169445e82ef1e16ead53e4c486","clm_3d3002806729950234aaffc9759ad092cfbd88ac69489d08cef8df52280d327b","clm_3e3425fb2166eb68f9fdb901185b35e92b3106eab6b25f1057027a73901f37c1","clm_4e78ed48a486b339474f3c80394ef7cb852392df2973ed88bd44f00e912a91e4","clm_6535b61aee64a46d6b5d041021467c3238e8df80651fc688e233d709c10108e2","clm_7558ec539179c9b0b5fb17d46dba15625093c92aca35bbcbfbbfb1866c250621","clm_89e6452e8b4e8fd72736a2a91c39c87bf02b8a3ac5d94656580e0409a83deccc","clm_8c52c55eccbd5b2c6970defb70c71ad8b502d7ea2e24c19825928526eb60a8e3","clm_970a78ae79337d59265c6517bb5db2f6b618efc17772bf26735c3df95c7e145b","clm_9a667136be04ff445a4314681169935c2946185001a53320c731d2f92174a6d3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","id":"pg_eb5cc7ca5f605bf49c6f7ef86223719b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/kenn-io-kata-docs-design-architecture-md-f41a33383aba-7ef86223719b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"title":"kenn-io/kata/docs/design/architecture.md @ f41a33383aba","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
